L2: /*
L3:  * apply.js - install / remove the DeepSeek dashboard into the OpenCode desktop app.
L4:  *
L5:  * Since v2 this addon shares a single append-only main entry, out/main/oc-addons.js,
L6:  * with the other addons (see whatsNew.md). install appends:
L7:  *   + out/main/deepseek-main.js      (login window + usage proxy)
L8:  *   + out/renderer/deepseek-panel.js (the panel UI)
L9:  *   + out/main/oc-addons.js          (shared loader, only if absent)
L10:  *   ~ package.json                   (main -> ./out/main/oc-addons.js)
L11:  *   ~ out/preload/index.js           (expose window.api.deepseek*)
L12:  *   ~ out/renderer/index.html        (<script src="./deepseek-panel.js">)
L13:  *
L14:  * Existing data is never moved (only appended), so original offsets stay valid.
L15:  * remove neutralizes this addon (its module becomes an empty stub) and strips
L16:  * its renderer script tag / preload lines, without touching other addons.
L17:  * restore-all copies the shared pristine backup back over app.asar.
L18:  * Run while OpenCode is closed.
L19:  *
L20:  *   node apply.js install|remove|restore-all|status|verify [--app <dir>] [--force]
L21:  */
